### Problem Details

**Problem 1: Slow ASP.NET Test Execution**

MSTest + Selenium = 10-30 minute feedback loop:

```csharp
// MSTest - Requires IIS, database, full app startup
[TestMethod]
public void TestClaimsSearch()
{
    var driver = new ChromeDriver();
    driver.Navigate().GoToUrl("http://localhost/claims");
    // Wait for ViewState, postbacks, etc.
    Thread.Sleep(2000);
    // Flaky assertions
}
```

Vitest + React Testing Library = <1 second:

```typescript
// Vitest - Pure JavaScript, no browser required
it('renders claims search form', () => {
  render(<ClaimsSearchForm />);
  expect(screen.getByLabelText('Claim ID')).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

**Problem 2: No Automated Accessibility Testing**

Manual accessibility testing is expensive and inconsistent. Automated tests catch 30-40% of issues.

**Problem 3: No Contract Testing**

Frontend and backend teams make breaking changes without visibility until integration.

