[patterns/application/micro-frontend/PTN-APP-MFE-015-testing-strategy-pattern.md#scenario-1-testing-complex-healthcare-workflow]

#### Scenario 1: Testing Complex Healthcare Workflow

**When to Use:** Prior authorization workflow with 5-step process, conditional logic, and external API calls

**Testing Approach:**

- **Unit Tests (60%)**: Test each step component in isolation, validation logic, conditional rendering
- **Integration Tests (30%)**: Test step transitions, state management, API mocking (MSW)
- **E2E Tests (10%)**: Test complete happy path and 2-3 critical error scenarios
- **Contract Tests**: Validate prior auth API request/response schema (Pact)

**Example:**

```typescript
// Unit test: Step 1 validation
it('requires diagnosis code before proceeding to step 2', async () => {
  const user = userEvent.setup();
  render(<Step1DiagnosisInfo onNext={mockNext} />);

  await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Next' }));

  expect(screen.getByText('Diagnosis code is required')).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(mockNext).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
});

// E2E test: Complete workflow
test('complete prior auth submission', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/prior-auth/new');

  // Step 1: Diagnosis
  await page.getByLabel('Diagnosis Code').fill('J06.9');
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Next' }).click();

  // Step 2: Procedure
  await page.getByLabel('CPT Code').fill('99213');
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Next' }).click();

  // ... Steps 3-5

  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' }).click();
  await expect(page.getByText('Prior authorization submitted')).toBeVisible();
});
```

