#### Scenario 3: Testing Accessibility Requirements

**When to Use:** Healthcare applications requiring Section 508/WCAG 2.2 AA compliance

**Testing Approach:**

- **Automated Tests (30-40%)**: axe-core in Playwright E2E tests
- **Keyboard Navigation Tests**: Tab order, focus management, keyboard shortcuts
- **Screen Reader Tests**: aria-labels, landmark regions, live regions
- **Manual Testing (60-70%)**: Human testers with assistive technology

**Example:**

```typescript
test('claims search is keyboard accessible', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/claims');

  // Tab to search input
  await page.keyboard.press('Tab');
  expect(await page.evaluate(() => document.activeElement?.id)).toBe('claim-search');

  // Type claim ID and press Enter
  await page.keyboard.type('CLM001');
  await page.keyboard.press('Enter');

  // Verify results loaded
  await expect(page.getByText('CLM001')).toBeVisible();
});
```
